#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-reflog(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:7
msgid "git-reflog - Manage reflog information"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"git reflog [show] [<log-options>] [<ref>]\n"
"git reflog list\n"
"git reflog exists <ref>\n"
"git reflog write <ref> <old-oid> <new-oid> <message>\n"
"git reflog delete [--rewrite] [--updateref]\n"
"\t[--dry-run | -n] [--verbose] <ref>@{<specifier>}...\n"
"git reflog drop [--all [--single-worktree] | <refs>...]\n"
"git reflog expire [--expire=<time>] [--expire-unreachable=<time>]\n"
"\t[--rewrite] [--updateref] [--stale-fix]\n"
"\t[--dry-run | -n] [--verbose] [--all [--single-worktree] | <refs>...]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:26
msgid "This command manages the information recorded in the reflogs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:34
msgid ""
"Reference logs, or \"reflogs\", record when the tips of branches and other "
"references were updated in the local repository. Reflogs are useful in "
"various Git commands, to specify the old value of a reference. For example, "
"`HEAD@{2}` means \"where HEAD used to be two moves ago\", "
"`master@{one.week.ago}` means \"where master used to point to one week ago "
"in this local repository\", and so on. See linkgit:gitrevisions[7] for more "
"details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:37
msgid ""
"The command takes various subcommands, and different options depending on "
"the subcommand:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:44
msgid ""
"The \"show\" subcommand (which is also the default, in the absence of any "
"subcommands) shows the log of the reference provided in the command-line (or "
"`HEAD`, by default). The reflog covers all recent actions, and in addition "
"the `HEAD` reflog records branch switching.  `git reflog show` is an alias "
"for `git log -g --abbrev-commit --pretty=oneline`; see linkgit:git-log[1] "
"for more information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:46
msgid "The \"list\" subcommand lists all refs which have a corresponding reflog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:50
msgid ""
"The \"exists\" subcommand checks whether a ref has a reflog.  It exits with "
"zero status if the reflog exists, and non-zero status if it does not."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:56
msgid ""
"The \"write\" subcommand writes a single entry to the reflog of a given "
"reference. This new entry is appended to the reflog and will thus become the "
"most recent entry. The reference name must be fully qualified. Both the old "
"and new object IDs must not be abbreviated and must point to existing "
"objects.  The reflog message gets normalized."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:61
msgid ""
"The \"delete\" subcommand deletes single entries from the reflog, but not "
"the reflog itself. Its argument must be an _exact_ entry (e.g. \"`git reflog "
"delete master@{2}`\"). This subcommand is also typically not used directly "
"by end users."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:65
msgid ""
"The \"drop\" subcommand completely removes the reflog for the specified "
"references. This is in contrast to \"expire\" and \"delete\", both of which "
"can be used to delete reflog entries, but not the reflog itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:71
msgid ""
"The \"expire\" subcommand prunes older reflog entries. Entries older than "
"`expire` time, or entries older than `expire-unreachable` time and not "
"reachable from the current tip, are removed from the reflog.  This is "
"typically not used directly by end users -- instead, see linkgit:git-gc[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:73
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "Options for `show`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:79
msgid "`git reflog show` accepts any of the options accepted by `git log`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:82
#, no-wrap
msgid "Options for `delete`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:87
msgid ""
"`git reflog delete` accepts options `--updateref`, `--rewrite`, `-n`, "
"`--dry-run`, and `--verbose`, with the same meanings as when they are used "
"with `expire`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "Options for `drop`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:91
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:103
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--all`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:93
msgid "Drop the reflogs of all references from all worktrees."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:94
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:106
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--single-worktree`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:98
msgid ""
"By default when `--all` is specified, reflogs from all working trees are "
"dropped. This option limits the processing to reflogs from the current "
"working tree only."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:101
#, no-wrap
msgid "Options for `expire`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:105
msgid "Process the reflogs of all references."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:110
msgid ""
"By default when `--all` is specified, reflogs from all working trees are "
"processed. This option limits the processing to reflogs from the current "
"working tree only."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:111
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--expire=<time>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:118
msgid ""
"Prune entries older than the specified time. If this option is not "
"specified, the expiration time is taken from the configuration setting "
"`gc.reflogExpire`, which in turn defaults to 90 days. `--expire=all` prunes "
"entries regardless of their age; `--expire=never` turns off pruning of "
"reachable entries (but see `--expire-unreachable`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:119
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--expire-unreachable=<time>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:128
msgid ""
"Prune entries older than `<time>` that are not reachable from the current "
"tip of the branch. If this option is not specified, the expiration time is "
"taken from the configuration setting `gc.reflogExpireUnreachable`, which in "
"turn defaults to 30 days. `--expire-unreachable=all` prunes unreachable "
"entries regardless of their age; `--expire-unreachable=never` turns off "
"early pruning of unreachable entries (but see `--expire`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:129
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--updateref`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:133
msgid ""
"Update the reference to the value of the top reflog entry (i.e.  "
"<ref>@\\{0\\}) if the previous top entry was pruned.  (This option is "
"ignored for symbolic references.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:134
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--rewrite`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:138
msgid ""
"If a reflog entry's predecessor is pruned, adjust its \"old\" SHA-1 to be "
"equal to the \"new\" SHA-1 field of the entry that now precedes it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:139
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--stale-fix`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:144
msgid ""
"Prune any reflog entries that point to \"broken commits\". A broken commit "
"is a commit that is not reachable from any of the reference tips and that "
"refers, directly or indirectly, to a missing commit, tree, or blob object."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:149
msgid ""
"This computation involves traversing all the reachable objects, i.e. it has "
"the same cost as 'git prune'.  It is primarily intended to fix corruption "
"caused by garbage collecting using older versions of Git, which didn't "
"protect objects referred to by reflogs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-n`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:151
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--dry-run`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:154
msgid "Do not actually prune any entries; just show what would have been pruned."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:155
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--verbose`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.adoc:157
msgid "Print extra information on screen."
msgstr ""

